Rust dependencies
-----------------

The cp0ctl binary and device services are built from Rust crates locked by
Cargo.lock. Cargo.lock is the authoritative name, version and checksum record
for every crates.io dependency used by a release. Each dependency is distributed
under the license declared in its published crate package; its authoritative
license text is available from the crate package at the locked version.

The CardputerZero release process must retain Cargo.lock and must not replace,
remove or relicense third-party Rust dependency notices. Before publishing a
binary artifact, release operators must generate and review a complete,
versioned Rust dependency license report from Cargo.lock and include all license
texts required by the resolved dependency set with the artifact.

Other bundled content
---------------------

App DevKit and Skill archives contain CardputerZero-authored SDK, documentation,
examples and Skill content under the repository Apache-2.0 license unless a
file carries a different notice. They do not include private keys, tokens,
passwords, proprietary Store data, or build-vendor source trees.

The device image may include assets and packages with additional notices. The
release pipeline must preserve package-level license and copyright information
from the finished image and must not represent this file as a substitute for
those notices.

Source and maintenance
----------------------

Update this file whenever a shipped third-party component, pin, linkage mode or
release payload changes. Do not add development-only dependencies unless they
are included in a distributed artifact. See app-runtime/THIRD-PARTY.md for the
Runtime-specific attribution record.
